==Tocharian B==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-toc-pro|txb}} {{m|ine-toc-pro|*meim}}, a nominal derivative of *''mei-'' ("to measure"). Possibly linked to {{etyl|ine-pro|txb}} *''mod-ye/o-'' or *''mēdye/o-'', derivatives of {{m|ine-pro|*med-||to measure, give advice, heal}} (whence Latin {{m|la|meditor}}), or alternatively to *''meh₁-ye/o-'' from {{m|ine-pro|*meh₁-||to measure}} (whence Latin {{m|la|mētior}}). Compare Tocharian A {{m|xto|mem}}.

